MEMORY_UPDATE/v1

project: SMARTROUTER / SECURITYMANAGER
training_case: FORGEJO_PRIVATE_REPOSITORY_PUBLICATION
source_issue: 175
successor_issue: 178
status: REAL_CREDENTIAL_RELATIONSHIP_FIXTURE

The Darwin Forgejo incident now cleanly separates:
- access plane: healthy through tailnet-only Serve;
- repository identity: chitakasha/gd2;
- desired capability: read + push non-protected branch + create PR;
- execution secret/session: must remain hidden;
- current result: unauthenticated probe returns HTTP 403.

#178 tests whether an existing Keychain/helper/client can exercise that capability opaquely. If absent, it must emit a provider/principal/repo/verbs-bound CAPABILITY_REQUEST/v1 with a fresh-process probe, not request a copied password or token. This is memory/training evidence, not authorization to implement SecurityManager or mint credentials.
